git commit -m "ADR-101: a click is not a result" -m "ADR-100 built a harness that discovered 3684 affordances and drove 2357 of them, and it asked every one of them a single question: did anything change. That question is answered yes by a plus button that subtracts, by a filter that keeps exactly the rows that do not match, by an option that bumps a counter and refuses to select, and by a Copy CSV that puts an empty string on the clipboard. The harness had established that the kit is wired. Reporting that as evidence the kit works was the over-claim in ADR-100 s headline number, and this retracts it." -m "tools/swarm.py keeps that harness s discovery and its accounting and replaces the oracle. Twelve expectations, each written in terms of what a user would see. A tab leaves exactly one pane open and it is the named one. A stepper moves in the direction its label promises. A field holds what was typed. A slider DISPLAYS the number it was set to. A select reports the option that was chosen. An option SELECTS when clicked, and alone in a radio group. A filter s survivors all match the query, some were removed, and clearing brings every one of them back. An add makes exactly one more row and a remove one fewer. A clear leaves fewer fields holding anything. An undo returns to a state this run has been in. An export leaves the page, PARSES, and contains what was typed into the form." -m "A control with no expectation attached is not called verified. It is called changed, which is the honest name for what ADR-100 was measuring, and the split between the two is the number this slice exists to print: discovered 3554 = verified 1966 + wrong 18 + changed 273 + dead 34 + hidden 204 + failed 4 + excluded 1055. 1984 of 2257 driven affordances were checked against a stated expectation, 87 percent. The 1966 break down as option 1168, field 321, step 236, tab 87, filter 40, add 29, export 23, remove 20, undo 18, slider 10, print 9, select 3, clear 2." -m "None of those questions can be asked of an empty page. An empty form exports an empty file perfectly correctly and a spore swatch pressed before a collection exists is right to do nothing, so a run now begins by entering a recorded sentinel into every text field, pressing every add-shaped button, and then every save-shaped one. Filling a form is not the same as having a record, and four exports were called wrong for exactly that difference before the seed learned to commit. The export oracle can then ask a question worth asking: is what the user typed in the file the page produced." -m "Nine defects were found in the instrument, every one by reading a wrong finding rather than by reasoning about the design. The verdict was being computed from a label the walk no longer pointed at: selectors are positional within a kind and these widgets rebuild, so by the time action_btn:30 was driven it was no longer the Copy .eco lines button discovered under that name, and an export oracle was applied to a quadrat arrow. That is ADR-100 s rebuild problem one layer up - the earlier fix stopped the walk TOUCHING an element that had vanished, and did not stop it JUDGING one control by another control s promise. Every control is now re-observed immediately before it is judged." -m "Second, a correct refusal read as a wrong result. An export with nothing saved, a swatch pressed too early, an Add with nothing selected - nineteen of the first thirty-five findings were controls declining exactly as they should. Judging a control from a state where its effect could not appear is the ADR-100 defect wearing the oracle s clothes. A refusal is now allowed on one condition, which is the rule this kit already holds itself to everywhere else: it has to TELL the user. A control that declines with a toast is doing its job. A control that declines in silence is indistinguishable from one that is broken, to the harness and to the person holding the phone, and stays a finding." -m "Third, the harness poisoned the widget it then failed to measure: a stepper holds a number and the walk was typing a text sentinel into it, so the next press computed NaN and the press after that computed NaN from NaN, and a live plus button reported as leaving no trace. Fourth, a toast raised while an identical toast is still on screen is not a mutation - the same blindness that cost ADR-100 twelve live controls - so raises are counted at the call now. Fifth, prose with commas in it was read as a ragged CSV, which called three of the kit s AI-prompt exports malformed tables; a payload is a table when most of its rows agree on a width of three or more." -m "Sixth, a filter was judged by a query that separates nothing - a picker with one option cannot be filtered below one, and a query every option matches correctly removes none. Seventh, a pane that no tab opens was counted as 54 undriveable controls on experiment-guide, because the harness insisted on a route that page does not use. Eighth, an element gone between the snapshot and the read was filed as a failure, inflating the one bucket that means this tool could not do its job; it is a fact about the page and belongs in hidden, and failed fell from 108 to 4. Ninth, show-pane refused before the oracle could report, asking whether a pane was THE open one rather than whether it had opened, so a page leaving two panes open came back as no such tab - a finding turned into a failure." -m "Two expectations were retracted as too strong for what a label can carry. A clear had been asserted to leave no field holding anything, and breeding-bench s Clear trial, correctly scoped to the trial, was reported as a defect for it; field-notebook s Reset resets a stopwatch and its Clear empties a quadrat list. A label says that something is cleared, not what. On the four-page pilot the first run reported 35 wrong results and the same four pages now report 7. Twenty-eight of the first thirty-five findings were mine." -m "tools/verify/verify_swarm.py writes ten fixture pages. Nine of them are wired, respond to every click, and would pass ADR-100 s oracle: a plus that subtracts, a filter that keeps what does not match, an option that will not select, a field that eats what is typed, a Copy that copies an empty string, a CSV whose rows disagree about the column count, a well-formed export of somebody else s data, a tab that opens a pane without closing the other, and an Add that changes a caption and adds no row. Each is asserted to be caught by its OWN oracle by name, not merely to produce some complaint. The tenth is entirely in order and the assertion on it is that nothing is reported, because an instrument that cannot come back clean is not measuring. The accounting identity is asserted on all ten. One fixture failed on its first run and the fixture was wrong, not the swarm - which is how the NaN defect above was found." -m "The swarm reaches the page through a typed action layer rather than clicking at everything and inferring afterwards: press-step with a direction, set-text with a value, choose-option with an option. That is what makes the oracles possible, because the harness knows what it asked for and can therefore say what it expected. The layer carries the safety properties that come with letting anything drive these pages automatically - off unless enabled, a token on every call, entered values withheld unless explicitly unlocked, generic activation treated as the most consequential thing a selector can mean, and a request id so a retried command does not operate the page twice. There is a 120-line stdio adapter, an operator page in docs/AUTOMATION-HARNESS.md, and 65 assertions in tools/verify/verify_contract.py. None of that is the point of the slice; the point is that 1966 controls were asked what they promise and answered." -m "Suite 63 of 63 jobs green, 4415 of 4415 checks passing (61 and 4322 before); verify_swarm 28/28 and verify_contract 65/65 are the new jobs. No page changed, nothing was republished, no staleness is owed. The swarm is not wired into run_all, for ADR-100 s reason: a red suite nobody can turn green gets ignored, which is how a gate becomes a decoration." -m "The worklist. Eighteen results that were not what the control promises: eleven exports, of which nine produce a well-formed payload containing none of the values entered even after a record was saved, one copies nothing and says nothing, and one emits a CSV where a row is not the width of the others; four Adds that add no row and raise no toast; two clears that change nothing at all; one Delete that removes nothing. Thirty-four affordances that left no trace, headed by fifteen of ethogram s behaviour buttons and five of farm-scout s bespoke minus arrows. ADR-100 s worklist is still open and untouched by this slice." -m "Next, and falsifiable. Everything above is a control answering wrongly. I claim the kit s DECLINES are in better shape than its actions - that where a control refuses it nearly always says so, because the toast is a house habit. I expect that to be wrong: at least five of the thirty-four affordances that left no trace are guarded controls declining in silence, doing nothing and saying nothing, and are being read as unwired when they are in fact refusing. The fifteen ethogram buttons are where I expect to find them. Falsifier: reading every one of the thirty-four against its handler and finding that each either has no guard at all or raises a toast."
